              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "luctor, luctārī — \"to wrestle, struggle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Iuvenēs in campō luctantur. The young men wrestle on the field."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deponent: luctor, luctārī, luctātus sum. Also to struggle against something. English reluctant comes from reluctor."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "luctor is built on lucta \"wrestling\" (Lewis & Short); EtymDB links it with a Proto-Indo-European root meaning \"to bend, twist\". English reluctant comes from the compound reluctor."
            }
          ]
        },
